  "body": "Part of #2238 (frame cost: calculate before and cache). Measured with the frame-cost probe of #2238, release build, fig8.step.\n\n## What happens\n\nThe parameter fields of a Contour operation call `camcraft_app::operation::contour_auto_side` (from `crates/ui/src/egui_app/params_page.rs`, `params_fields`) on each frame, to show the side that Auto resolves to. No input changed between the frames.\n\n| State | Piece | ms per frame (release) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Contour on 10 top edge chains | `ui/properties.op.fields.contour_auto_side` | 4.13 |\n\n## Done means\n\n- The resolved side is calculated when the picks, the parameters, the setup or the model change, and read from a cache on other frames.\n- The cache is in `app`, next to `contour_auto_side`. The key follows `docs/decisions/2238-frame-cost-rule.md`. Do not key it on `doc_version` alone.\n- A counter test: a still frame makes zero new calculations.\n- A changed-input test: a changed chain pick gives the new side, equal to a fresh calculation.\n- The generator and the post do not read this cache. The side that the toolpath uses is not changed.\n- The probe `frame_cost_probe` shows the piece under 0.1 ms in release.\n",
